## Produce and verify a content assertion

A content assertion is a second sibling attestation profile: a standalone compact JWS
(`typ: "ba+content-assertion"`) that binds the digest of exact external content bytes to an
issuer, audience, lineage subject, semantic profile, validity window, and predecessor. The
package hashes the bytes you pass and never parses them; what the content means stays with you.

```elixir
notebook_value = (
  alias BoundedAuthorityProtocol.ContentAssertion.V1, as: ContentAssertionV1

  {content_attestor_public, content_attestor_private} = :crypto.generate_key(:eddsa, :ed25519)

  content_bytes = ~s({"document":"example","revision":1})
  {:ok, content_digest} = ContentAssertionV1.content_digest(content_bytes, %{})

  # The semantic profile's identity is a caller-pinned opaque 32-byte digest:
  profile_digest = :crypto.hash(:sha256, "urn:example:profile:document/1 schema bytes")

  assertion = %ContentAssertionV1.ContentAssertion{
    attestor_key_id: "content-attestor-1",
    jti: "urn:example:assertion:2026-001",
    iss: "urn:example:issuer",
    aud: "urn:example:audience",
    sub: "urn:example:lineage:document-1",
    profile: "urn:example:profile:document/1",
    profile_digest: profile_digest,
    content_digest: content_digest,
    gen: 1,
    prev: <<0::256>>,
    iat: now,
    nbf: now,
    exp: now + 3_600
  }

  {:ok, assertion_input} = ContentAssertionV1.assertion_signing_input(assertion, %{})

  assertion_signature =
    :crypto.sign(:eddsa, :none, assertion_input.message, [content_attestor_private, :ed25519])

  {:ok, assertion_compact} =
    ContentAssertionV1.assemble_compact(assertion_input, assertion_signature)

  expected_assertion = %ContentAssertionV1.ExpectedContentAssertion{
    attestor: %HistoricalPublicKey{
      key_id: "content-attestor-1",
      public_key: content_attestor_public,
      valid_from: now - 600,
      valid_before: now + 7_200
    },
    issuer: "urn:example:issuer",
    audience: "urn:example:audience",
    subject: "urn:example:lineage:document-1",
    profile: "urn:example:profile:document/1",
    profile_digest: profile_digest,
    content_digest: content_digest,
    now: now + 60,
    bounds: %{}
  }

  {:ok, assertion_facts} =
    ContentAssertionV1.verify_assertion(assertion_compact, expected_assertion)

  Map.take(Map.from_struct(assertion_facts), [:attestor_key_id, :sub, :gen, :verification, :trust])
)
true = notebook_value === (
  %{attestor_key_id: "content-attestor-1", sub: "urn:example:lineage:document-1", gen: 1, verification: :signature_and_window, trust: :not_evaluated}
)
notebook_value
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{attestor_key_id: "content-attestor-1", sub: "urn:example:lineage:document-1", gen: 1, verification: :signature_and_window, trust: :not_evaluated}
```

The cell returns `%{attestor_key_id: "content-attestor-1", sub: "urn:example:lineage:document-1", gen: 1, verification: :signature_and_window, trust: :not_evaluated}`.

Generation 2 names generation 1 by the SHA-256 of its exact compact bytes. The pairwise check
compares two verified facts values; it keeps no history of its own.

```elixir
notebook_value = (
  successor = %{
    assertion
    | jti: "urn:example:assertion:2026-002",
      gen: 2,
      prev: assertion_facts.digest,
      iat: now + 120,
      nbf: now + 120
  }

  {:ok, successor_input} = ContentAssertionV1.assertion_signing_input(successor, %{})

  successor_signature =
    :crypto.sign(:eddsa, :none, successor_input.message, [content_attestor_private, :ed25519])

  {:ok, successor_compact} =
    ContentAssertionV1.assemble_compact(successor_input, successor_signature)

  {:ok, successor_facts} =
    ContentAssertionV1.verify_assertion(successor_compact, %{expected_assertion | now: now + 180})

  ContentAssertionV1.verify_successor(assertion_facts, successor_facts, %{})
)
true = notebook_value === (
  :ok
)
notebook_value
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
:ok
```

The cell returns `:ok`: generation 2 follows generation 1.

## Content-assertion attacks fail closed

```elixir
notebook_value = (
  {:ok, changed_digest} = ContentAssertionV1.content_digest(content_bytes <> " ", %{})

  %{
    # One changed content byte changes the digest the verifier requires:
    changed_content:
      ContentAssertionV1.verify_assertion(assertion_compact, %{
        expected_assertion
        | content_digest: changed_digest
      }),
    # now == exp: the acceptance window is the half-open [nbf, exp).
    now_at_exp:
      ContentAssertionV1.verify_assertion(assertion_compact, %{expected_assertion | now: now + 3_600}),
    # Lineage runs forward only:
    reversed_lineage: ContentAssertionV1.verify_successor(successor_facts, assertion_facts, %{}),
    # Other profiles refuse content-assertion bytes:
    assertion_through_role: RoleAttestationV1.decode_attestation(assertion_compact, %{}),
    assertion_through_major_one: BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.decode_grant(assertion_compact, %{})
  }
)
true = notebook_value === (
  %{
    changed_content: {:error, :invalid},
    now_at_exp: {:error, :invalid},
    reversed_lineage: {:error, :invalid},
    assertion_through_role: {:error, :invalid},
    assertion_through_major_one: {:error, :invalid}
  }
)
notebook_value
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  changed_content: {:error, :invalid},
  now_at_exp: {:error, :invalid},
  reversed_lineage: {:error, :invalid},
  assertion_through_role: {:error, :invalid},
  assertion_through_major_one: {:error, :invalid}
}
```

A content assertion proves that a key you trust signed this exact digest and context. It does
not prove that the content is true, that the key is still trusted, or that you hold the latest
generation. Trusted keys, durable lineage state, and replay handling stay with the caller.
